# Line endings. The shell scripts, the ANGLE lock and the GN args are read
# by bash / gn on Windows runners, where Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true and would otherwise check them out CRLF (the first
# windows.yml run refused config/angle.lock because every value carried a
# trailing carriage return). Keep them LF everywhere; PowerShell 7 reads
# LF scripts fine, so nothing needs CRLF.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.gnargs text eol=lf
*.c text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
config/angle.lock text eol=lf
